abstract:
We report final results on electroweak parameters from muon-neutrino electron scattering observed in the CHARM II detector from 1987 till 1991. In total $2677 \pm 82$ and $2752 \pm 88$ neutrino-electron scattering events have been detected in the $
u$ and $ ar{
u}$ beam, respectively. From the ratio of differential cross sections we obtain for the electroweak mixing angle $\sin^{2}\Theta = 0.2324 \pm 0.0083$. From the absolute neutrino-electron scattering event rate we determined the effective vector and axial-vector neutral current coupling constants to be $g_V^{
u e} = -0.035 \pm 0.017$ and $g_A^{
u e} = -0.503 \pm 0.017$.
